\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. When morning gilds The skies,
\par My heart awaking cries:
\par May Jesus Christ be praised!
\par Alike at work and prayer
\par To Jesus I repair:
\par May Jesus Christ be praised!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Does sadness fill my mind?
\par A solace here I find-
\par May Jesus Christ be praised!
\par When evil thoughts molest,
\par With this I shield my breast-
\par May Jesus Christ be praised!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Be this, when day is past, 
\par Of all my thoughts the last,
\par May Jesus Christ be praised!
\par The night becomes as day,
\par When from the heart we say:
\par May Jesus Christ be praised!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. To God, the Word, on high
\par The hosts of angels cry,
\par May Jesus Christ be praised!
\par Let mortals, too, upraise
\par Their voice in hymns of praise:
\par May Jesus Christ be praised!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Let earth's wide circle round
\par In joyful notes resound:
\par May Jesus Christ be praised!
\par Let air, and sea, and sky,
\par From depth to height, reply:
\par May Jesus Christ be praised!
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par \'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Be this while life is mine,
\par My canticle divine,
\par May Jesus Christ be praised!
\par Be this the eternal song
\par Through all the ages long,
\par May Jesus Christ be praised!
\par                                   Amen.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

